       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Many references use 2,000 mg/day as the practical ceiling.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day, usually given once daily.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a more typical regimen\n\nTell me the dose you want, and please confirm it with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, I'd want the attending to confirm that explicitly first."
      }
